name smart-eqn
category Package
revision 61719
shortdesc Automatic math symbol styling for LaTeX documents
longdesc In LaTeX typesetting, one usually needs to use different
longdesc variants of a math symbol to clarify the meanings. For example,
longdesc in linear algebra literature, it is common to use boldfaced
longdesc symbols to represent vectors, and normal symbols to represent
longdesc scalars. However, applying these variants by typing \mathbf,
longdesc \mathrm commands manually can be daunting. This package aims to
longdesc provide an automatic and customizable approach for math symbol
longdesc styling which eliminates the need to enter style commands
longdesc repeatedly.
